{title: Riches of His Kindness}
{subtitle: Romans 2:4}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
You sit in judgment on another
Condemning them for what they do
But you the judge do the same [F#]
[C#]No excuse remains for [D#m]you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
God's judgment comes according to truth
On those who act in such a way
Do you think you will [F#]escape
[C#]When you judge others [D#m]day by day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Do you despise [F#]the riches of his kindness
[C#]Forbearance and patience [D#m]toward you
Not realizing his [F#]kindness
[C#]Is meant to lead you to [D#m]repentance
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Stubborn heart and unrepentant soul
You store up wrath for yourself
For the day of wrath is com[F#]ing
When his right[C#]eous judgment will be re[D#m]vealed
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[B]He will repay [C#]each one
[D#m]According to their works [F#]alone
[B]Eternal life for patient endu[C#]rance
Seeking [A#m]glory and honor in God
{end_of_bridge}

{comment: Interlude}
| [D#m] | [F#] | [C#] | [D#m] | ×2

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
His kindness leads you to re[F#]pentance
[C#]Turn away from your [D#m]stubborn ways
His kindness leads you to re[F#]pentance
[C#]Seek his glory in your [D#m]days
{end_of_verse}
